2024..2098 Comment "/// A path at every loop whose inverse arm drops its rest\'s path: each arm"
2099..2180 Comment "/// checks at its letter, but at `loop ∷ back(loop) ∷ q` the loop arm carries"
2181..2261 Comment "/// the inverse arm\'s reflexivity to `here(loop ∷ back(loop) ∷ q)`, which is"
2262..2337 Comment "/// not the path at `q` the cancellation\'s right side reads. Read as a set,"
2338..2406 Comment "/// the loops would identify the two; the words are not read as one."
